{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1156020-launguage-for-mortal-magic","id":1156020,"title":"launguage for mortal magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-05T05:36:08-08:00","id":1156020,"title":"launguage for mortal magic","content":"first snake and Dan ,if you're on these fourums, don't read this, spoilers and all that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> right for the game I'm running i want to include a book, that the players may or may not find, that will instruct them in 3 dot Pyrokynesis, I don't want the book to be in English, I don't want it to be to easy for to work out, it'll be a book of obvious importance, but undecipherable, and if they want to work it out first they need to work out the language then learn the language then study the book to gain access to the merit.<br /> <br /> the character who has the book is of eastern European heritage, not decided specifically what country yet, anyhow i want the book to be in a dead or disused language from that part of the world, but i don't know what language to use, can anyone with a greater knowledge of Slavic culture and language give me any pointers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T06:05:04-08:00","id":1156025,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia has a page on Slavic Languages that lists them with a good number of extinct languages.<br /> <br /> That said, depending on the age of the book, pretty much everything will be a dead language. It'll be impenetrable without specialist training, doubly so if it's handwritten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T07:15:35-08:00","id":1156040,"title":"","content":"If you go East European, don't discount East Germanic language (Burgundian, Goth (Ostrogoth, Visigoths etc.), Vandals, etc.), nor older languages such as Dacian or Thracian.<br /> <br /> For Slavic languages, here is the above mentioned page: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slavic_languages\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slavic_languages</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T10:13:17-08:00","id":1156082,"title":"","content":"Eh, it really depends on the Europe part you're considering and the historical period the mage lived in.<br /> I'd say to check out Old Polish or Old Church Slavonic and see if they can appeal you; otherwise the ex-jugoslavia and the regions around the Black Sea also have a strong Roman and Ottoman inheritage, so it would make sense for the book to be in latin too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T10:32:28-08:00","id":1156090,"title":"","content":"honestly i had not thought much about the origins of the book, for the moment (so unless you have a better idea) i have gone with the character being a second generation Ukrainian immigrant (game is set in London UK), the language the book is in old east Slavic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T11:58:43-08:00","id":1156107,"title":"","content":"Really, it depends <b>how old </b>the book is - for example, in Poland we did not have our own, separate written version of language from just Latin transcription until 1200s and written Polish language was not used widely until Miko\u0142aj's Rej critique in poem in year 1562 '<a href=\"https://pl.wikiquote.org/wiki/A_niechaj_narodowie_w%C5%BCdy_postronni_znaj%C4%85\" target=\"_blank\">Polacy nie g\u0119si, i\u017c sw\u00f3j j\u0119zyk maj\u0105</a>.' - So even occult stuff before years 1300 written in Polish are not very plausible, but between 1300 and 1562 Polish is much more 'vulgar language' you do not use beside making accounts, inventory lists, etc. Latin is language you write 'important stuff', like law or religion texts. Czech and Slovakia has similar language histories, more or less.<br /> <br /> Ukraine, as country much more on East, had taken Russian <a href=\"http://Cyrillic_script\" target=\"_blank\">Cyrillic script system</a> and had written version of their dialect from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_language#Literature_and_the_Ukrainian_literary_language\" target=\"_blank\">12th century.</a><br /> <br /> The first ever used written Slavic language - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Church_Slavonic\" target=\"_blank\">Old Church Slavonic</a> - was made to convert first Slavic countries to Eastern Christianity by Byzantine monks and apostles, circa 860's. It used even earlier than Cyrillic script system - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glagolitic_script\" target=\"_blank\">Glagolitic script</a> - that looks now very exotic, even for day to day users of Slavic languages from under Russian influences. If choosing truly occult written script - I would go with Glagolitic.<br /> <br /> There are some theories there could be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Christian_Slavic_writing\" target=\"_blank\">written system for pagan Slavic languages</a>, but it's not supported by any strong evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-05-2017, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:34:28-08:00","id":1156120,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info, the wiki pages on the linguistic history of the region and the Slavic languages is bit impenetrable. yeah Glogolitic script does look groovy, works for my purposes, wanted something to use other than Enochian or Greek or Latin, wanted something a little less cliche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:43:47-08:00","id":1156127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1156020-launguage-for-mortal-magic?p=1156120#post1156120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah Glogolitic script does look groovy, works for my purposes, wanted something to use other than Enochian or Greek or Latin, wanted something a little less cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glogolitic is partially inspired by Greek writing, but it looks fantastic-like and is very much Slavic as it can only be. So here you go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}